    "lemoon_guide": {
      "index": "In this guide",
      "help_title": "Find your next frame.",
      "help_body": "Check each model’s options and dimensions. If you need guidance, get in touch before choosing.",
      "catalogue": "Explore frames",
      "contact": "Ask our team",
      "measurements": {
        "title": "How to measure your glasses",
        "intro": "Start with glasses that feel comfortable and a ruler marked in millimeters. Check the temple code, take any missing measurements and compare them with the frame you are considering.",
        "visual_title": "Three measurements, in millimetres.",
        "visual_copy": "Lens width · bridge · temple length. The drawing identifies frame parts; it is not a size scale.",
        "step_1_title": "1. Read the temple code",
        "step_1_body_html": "<p>Open the temple arms and look for a series of numbers on the inside. A temple arm is the part that reaches behind your ear. On some frames, three numbers indicate lens width, bridge width and temple length, in that order and in millimeters.</p>",
        "step_2_title": "2. Measure the frame in millimeters",
        "step_2_body_html": "<p>Work with your actual glasses and write down each measurement with its name. Look straight at the front and align the ruler with the part you are measuring; avoid taking the reading diagonally.</p><p>In this diagram, overall width runs from one outside edge of the front to the other. It is not the same as measuring between the hinges. Check that the measurements you compare use the same endpoints, and do not calculate overall width by adding the two lenses and the bridge: the frame edges also take up space.</p>",
        "step_3_title": "3. Compare measurements on the product page",
        "step_3_body_html": "<p>On the product page of the frame you are considering, open the “Measurements” tab. Keep your notes nearby and compare one measurement at a time, always in the same unit.</p><ul><li>Match the measurement names and endpoints: lens width with lens width, overall width with overall width.</li><li>Use only the measurements available for that model. If one is missing, do not infer it from the photo, drawing or size label.</li><li>A written size such as small or medium does not replace measurements in millimeters or fill in missing values.</li></ul>",
        "step_3_note_html": "<p>If the measurements do not exactly match your favorite glasses, check which part differs and by how many millimeters. A wider front takes up more space across your face; a taller lens changes the vertical proportions. The measurements and shape of the bridge and temple arms influence how the frame rests and stays in place. A small difference does not, on its own, rule out a frame: compare each measurement and look at the shapes in the product photos.</p>",
        "help_title": "Missing a measurement?",
        "help_body_html": "<p>If a marking is unreadable, a product measurement is missing or you do not have glasses to compare, ask before choosing. Include the model and the measurement you need clarified.</p>"
      },
      "face": {
        "title": "Your style has more than one shape.",
        "intro": "Explore proportions, colours and silhouettes freely. Face shape can be a reference without becoming a rule for choosing frames.",
        "visual_title": "One reference, many possibilities.",
        "visual_copy": "Look at frame width, height and lines. What you enjoy and how it feels matter too.",
        "step_1_title": "Start with what you like",
        "step_1_body": "Think about a frame you enjoy wearing: soft or defined lines, subtle or standout colours. Explore a different silhouette when you want a change; you do not need to fit a face-shape category.",
        "step_2_title": "Look at proportions",
        "step_2_body": "Compare the model’s width and height with your current frame. Check its photos and dimensions to explore how much space it occupies on your face. Shape labels are a starting point.",
        "step_3_title": "Make room for comfort",
        "step_3_body": "Consider support at the bridge and temple length alongside style. A virtual try-on, when available, provides a visual reference and does not confirm physical fit. Ask us if you are unsure about a measurement."
      },
      "order": {
        "title": "Choose. Review. Place your order.",
        "intro": "Every selection matters, from the catalogue to checkout. This guide helps you review the product’s actual options and your total before buying.",
        "visual_title": "Your selection, step by step.",
        "visual_copy": "The price belongs to your selected variant. Review cart details and the conditions shown at checkout.",
        "step_1_title": "Explore and choose a model",
        "step_1_body": "Open a catalogue product and review its photos, dimensions and availability. Choose a colour and the options shown on its page. Your selection may change the variant and its price.",
        "step_2_title": "Review what you add to the cart",
        "step_2_body": "If the product offers lenses, follow its configuration and complete only the requested information. To buy a frame only, use that option when available. Review the variant, quantity, details and subtotal in your cart.",
        "step_3_title": "Confirm your details at checkout",
        "step_3_body": "You can buy as a guest without signing in. Continue from your cart to Shopify checkout and review your contact information, address, available shipping options and payment methods. Check the total and displayed conditions before confirming your order."
      },
      "try_on": {
        "title": "See how it could look.",
        "intro": "Virtual try-on depends on each product and a connected provider. Check the model’s page to see whether this option is available.",
        "visual_title": "Photos and dimensions help too.",
        "visual_copy": "A digital visualisation is a style reference. It does not confirm size or replace checking the physical fit of a frame.",
        "step_1_title": "Check whether the model offers try-on",
        "step_1_body": "Open the product page and look for virtual try-on. Access appears only when the model has a configured link; not every product includes it.",
        "step_2_title": "Read the provider’s instructions",
        "step_2_body": "If a try-on service is connected, read its instructions and privacy terms before using it. Permissions and requirements depend on that service. The store does not need camera access to browse the catalogue.",
        "step_3_title": "Without try-on, compare other references",
        "step_3_body": "Use the model’s photos, dimensions and a frame you already find comfortable. If you need help with a measurement or product options, ask the team before choosing."
