      "lens_width": "Measure one lens from side to side at its widest point, keeping the ruler horizontal. Do not include the surrounding rim or the bridge gap.",
      "bridge": "Measure the shortest gap between the inner edges of the two lenses at the bridge. Do not measure on your nose or confuse this distance with the outside width of the frame’s bridge piece.",
      "lens_height": "Measure one lens from top to bottom at its tallest point, keeping the ruler vertical. Leave out the rim: this describes the lens, not the height of the entire front.",
      "temple": "Follow the temple arm from the hinge to the tip, including the curve behind your ear. A flexible tape marked in millimeters can help you follow that path. Do not bend or straighten the arm to measure it."
